# Solo Scrum (Jira in the browser)

The developer runs Jira **themselves**. Do **not** create, edit, or close Jira work unless they explicitly say OK for that ticket.

Stay on **Jira Cloud Free**. Do **not** suggest upgrading to Standard, turning on **Rovo**, or reconnecting the Atlassian MCP. Those cost money or time and are not needed to plan Version 1.

## Order of work

1. **Epic** — one big goal (example: User management API).
2. **User stories** — useful slices under that epic. Keep only the next 2–3 open. Do not dump a huge backlog.
3. **Sprint** — 1 week. Pull 1–4 stories. Unfinished stories move to the next sprint (normal, not failure).
4. **Tasks** — coding steps. Add them **last**, and **only** for stories already in the current sprint.

Skip team theatre: no daily standup, no story points, no burndown charts.

## Done

For API work, a story is Done when it works in **Postman**. Then they code the next story.

When they ask what to put in Jira, show short paste-ready titles in chat. They click in Jira.

## Why this option

Solo Scrum is a short list plus a weekly box. Paying for Rovo only so AI can click Jira is not worth it on a salary budget.
